[size=4][b]Introduction[/b][/size]
Inspired by [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/3394]Runes Clock[/url] — this mod gives you 25 runes every 5 seconds just from playing normally, and the longer you play, the more you get thanks to time-based milestone bonuses. Everything is configurable.

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]By default you get +25 runes every 5 seconds.[/*]
[*]The longer you stay in a single session, the bigger the milestone bonuses at 30 minutes, 1 hour, 2 hours, 3 hours, 6 hours, 12 hours, and 24 hours.[/*]
[*]Rune gain rate and milestone bonuses can all be adjusted in [b]PassiveRunes.ini[/b].[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[u][b]Option 1 — Using ModEngine2 (recommended)[/b][/u]
[list=1]
[*]Create a folder to hold the mod, e.g. name it [b]mod[/b].[/*]
[*]Copy [b]PassiveRunes.dll[/b] and [b]PassiveRunes.ini[/b] into that folder.[/*]
[*]Open [b]config_eldenring.toml[/b], find the [b]external_dlls[/b] entry and add it, e.g.: [b]mod\\PassiveRunes.dll[/b].[/*]
[*]Launch [b]modengine2_launcher.exe[/b].[/*]
[/list]

[u][b]Option 2 — Using Mod Loader[/b][/u]
[list=1]
[*]Download [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/117]Mod Loader[/url] and drop it into the game's install folder.[/*]
[*]Drag [b]PassiveRunes.dll[/b] and [b]PassiveRunes.ini[/b] into the [b]mods[/b] folder.[/*]
[*]Launch the game as usual.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#FF0000]Warning: [/color][/b][/size][b][color=#FF0000]Only use in offline mode with EAC disabled![/color][/b]

[size=4][b]Configuration (PassiveRunes.ini)[/b][/size]
[code][General]
; Key that reloads this file while the game is running.
ReloadKey=F5

[Rune Reward]
; Enable/disable this feature
Rune.Passive.Enabled=true

; How often it triggers, in milliseconds. Example: 1000=1 second, 500=0.5 second.
Rune.Passive.Interval=10000

; Amount of runes granted per interval
Rune.Passive.Amount=100

; Bonus runes at time milestones, formatted as (seconds:runes)
; Leave empty to disable the milestone bonuses
Rune.Milestone=1800:5000,3600:10000,7200:25000,10800:40000,21600:100000,43200:500000,86400:1000000

[Debug]
; Logs the Rune Reward module's activity. Only turn this on when you need to check something - it's noisy.
RuneLog=false[/code]

